       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg in one administration is above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n1. **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n2. **1,700 mg per day in total,** for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n3. **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n4. **1700 mg three times daily is intended.** If so, please confirm explicitly, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed.\n\nI'll enter the order once you confirm."
